<h2>Planning the circuit</h2>
<p>Path lights are low-wattage, but a long walk with a dozen fixtures still needs proper wire sizing to avoid voltage drop at the far end, where dim fixtures make spacing look uneven. Run the math with our <a href="/tools/transformer-sizing-calculator/">transformer sizing calculator</a>, or estimate the overall layout with the <a href="/tools/fixture-estimator/">fixture estimator</a>. If your existing path lights are dim, uneven or tilted, our <a href="/services/landscape-lighting-repair/">repair team</a> can reset and rebalance them.</p>
<p>At Spring Landscape Lighting we treat path lighting as one layer in a larger plan, so the walk feels connected to the house, trees and garden around it.</p>

